# Fictional accent authoring template for issue #135 (schema 1).
# Starfall (sc) is an invented conlang; this profile models a Starfall speaker
# rendering English (en). It is an authoring template, not a transcription.
# Replace checksum PLACEHOLDER with the value printed by --inspect-accent
# before sharing or rendering this file.
schema 1
name Starfall accent template
author Formant contributors
description Fictional Starfall-on-English accent: dental stops, recentred vowels, final devoicing and s-cluster epenthesis
license AGPL-3.0-or-later
version 1.0.0

accent starfall-on-en sc en
about starfall-on-en Invented conlang demonstration: nearest native segments, five-vowel quality, utterance-final devoicing and a vowel before s clusters
prosody starfall-on-en 1.02 0.92 1.04 0.96
rhythm starfall-on-en syllable

# Ordered maps: first match wins. Full substitutes are 1.0; intermediate
# strengths blend formants rather than replacing segment identity outright.
map starfall-on-en th t 0.9 any
map starfall-on-en dh d 0.9 any
map starfall-on-en æ /a/ 0.8 any
# Final devoicing: only the last spoken segment is eligible.
map starfall-on-en z s 1.0 final

# Cluster epenthesis: insert a short schwa before s when a consonant follows
# it in the same word. Inserted segments are tagged source=accent:starfall-on-en
# so the neural layer (#177) skips them.
insert starfall-on-en before s ə 0.7 cluster

# One per-phoneme override: shift all four formant centres and bandwidths,
# lengthen slightly, and leave pitch and amplitude untouched.
override starfall-on-en r 90 1.08 1.0 1.0

checksum PLACEHOLDER
